/**
 * Splits an amount (above 0.00 and below the claim's) off an OPEN claim not deferred past the sheet's today: the claim
 * keeps the rest and loses any figure a statement bound it to; a new OPEN claim with the amount, the same date and note,
 * the next number, opened by the user, split from the claim's number and due by the terms-th business day after its date,
 * with the terms in force for its person on the sheet's today, the day it is created (their own, else their grade's on that day, else the sheet's), is listed as the person's newest;
 * a late entry when that due-by is in a soft-closed period.
 */
// count by one and its count of that kind; while the sheet has proof kinds, one above the threshold needs a proof of each; one whose due is above the proof threshold
// in force on its date cannot be settled or approved while it has none (refused before the clerk limit is considered).
// An OPEN claim (not deferred, not in a closed period) can be split: an amount above 0.00 and below its own goes to a new
// OPEN claim with the next number, listed as the person's newest and showing the claim's number as split-from.
// An OPEN claim can be part-settled: the amount is split off as a split does and the new claim settled at once as a settle
// does (PENDING under the clerk limit), with the four-eyes and proof rules judged on the original; either refusal refuses all.
// A steward can re-date an OPEN or PENDING claim (not to a date after its person's retirement, nor one in a closed
60:    public boolean allows(String sheetId, String action, String role) {
61-        String value = find(sheetId, Setting.PERMISSION + action);
62-        List<String> roles = value == null ? Setting.PERMISSION_STANDING.get(action) : List.of(value.split(","));
63-        return roles.contains(role);
64-    }
65-
66-    /** A person's due-total held to the cap: the cap when it is above it; n/a (null) and no cap leave it as it is. */
67-    public static BigDecimal capped(BigDecimal dueTotal, BigDecimal cap) {
68-        return dueTotal == null || cap == null || dueTotal.compareTo(cap) <= 0 ? dueTotal : cap;
69-    }
70-
71-    /** The sheet's policy date: the one set, else its today. */
72-    public LocalDate policyDate(String sheetId, LocalDate today) {
73-        String value = find(sheetId, Setting.POLICY_DATE);
74-        return value == null ? today : LocalDate.parse(value);
75-    }

